        },
        "texto": "We have no account of the material or shape of the pak, which is here called “box,” and in 1 Samuel 10:1 “vial.” Gesenius derives it from pakah, to drop. This would seem to indicate a flask with a narrow mouth, from which oil or perfumery might be dropped. Such flasks have been f…"
      },
      "c-e81a0b224760575a": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-342",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "This is literally, “put her eyes in paint,” and alludes to the very ancient custom, still observed in the East, of coloring the eyes with a black powder called kohl. Graham says: “It is probable that stibium or antimony was formerly used for this purpose, and in some places it ma…"
      }
